course: dictionary
lesson: 2555
title: Words from dinosaur lessons
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are very specific, so the context has to tell you what they are. Look for clues around the word. In «The real Velociraptor was about the size of a turkey and had feathers; the film raptors were based on a bigger relative, Deinonychus.», the words «the film raptors were based on» show that Deinonychus is an animal, and «bigger relative» tells you it is a larger animal in the same family.
explain: The name is a clue too. Deinonychus means «terrible claw», so you can guess the animal had a claw that was special. Check your guess by putting the meaning into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: Read on for more clues. If a word is still unclear, skip it, read the rest of the text, and come back to it. The other sentences often explain it.
fact: Deinonychus was a meat-eating dinosaur about 3 metres long.
fact: It ran on two legs and had a large curved claw on each foot.
fact: Scientists think it was a fast, active hunter, and it probably had feathers.
fact: It lived in North America about 115 million years ago.
fact: In stories and films, the fast, clever «raptors» were inspired by it.
exercise: What kind of animal was Deinonychus? | *A meat-eating dinosaur | A small mammal that lived in trees | A kind of bird that could not fly
exercise: What does the name Deinonychus mean? | Long neck | *Terrible claw | Fast runner | Big feathers
exercise: «The film raptors were based on a bigger relative, Deinonychus.» What does relative most likely mean here? | A dinosaur with no feathers | A kind of claw | A rival that hunts the same food | *An animal closely related to another, like a cousin
test: Where did Deinonychus live? | In Africa, 65 million years ago | In Asia, last year | *In North America, about 115 million years ago | In Antarctica, 2 million years ago
test: What did Deinonychus have on each foot? | Four webbed toes | A horn on its nose | *A large curved claw | A thick shell
exam: Scientists say Deinonychus was closely related to birds; what does related mean here? | Hungry all the time | *Connected by family, like cousins | Born in the same year | Able to fly
